            <div xml:id="d475">

                <pb facs="0647" n="523" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg523"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">195.2/2701: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul in Chargé at Canton</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Price</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shameen</hi> (<hi rendition="#small-caps">Canton</hi>)</placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1921-05-26T15:00:00+08:00"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">May 26, 1921—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received
                        May 27—1:16 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>American companies operating under charter Chinese-owned vessels plying inland
                    waters desire to fly the flag of the United States at the masthead to indicate
                    charter interests, the vessels continuing <pb facs="0648" n="524" xml:id="pg524"
                    /> fly the flag of China aft and remain operating Chinese registry, Chinese
                    authorities acquiescing and other nationals permitted. Does the Department
                    sanction or prohibit? Please reply by telegraph as early as possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Price</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
